---
import Layout from "../Base.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Kelp Creative Agency handles website visits, Netlify form submissions, meeting bookings, blog comments, and website checker information."
>
  <article class="wrapper wrapper--narrow privacy-policy">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-05">October 5, 2026</time></p>
    <p>
      Kelp Creative Agency ("Kelp," "we," "us," or "our") operates
      <a href="https://www.kelp.agency/">www.kelp.agency</a>. This policy explains
      what information we collect through this website, why we use it, and how
      you can contact us about your privacy. It covers our website and related
      inquiries, bookings, comments, and website checks.
    </p>

    <h2>Information you provide</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Website package inquiries:</strong> your name, email address,
        requested additions, and the package and included services associated with your request.</li>
      <li><strong>Website checker requests:</strong> your name, work email address,
        website URL, and, when an automated check runs, its report ID and report URL.</li>
      <li><strong>Meeting bookings:</strong> the contact information, meeting time,
        and any answers or details you provide through our HubSpot booking tool.</li>
      <li><strong>Blog comments:</strong> your name, email address, comment, and the
        article you comment on. Comments are submitted to our WordPress system.
        Your display name and comment may appear publicly with a date and avatar;
        your email address is not displayed in the comment listing.</li>
      <li><strong>Direct communications:</strong> information you choose to share
        when you email, call, or otherwise contact us.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Please avoid including passwords, payment card details, or sensitive
      personal information in forms, comments, or website checker requests.</p>

    <h2>Hosting and form submissions</h2>
    <p>
      Netlify hosts this website and processes our website package and website
      checker forms through Netlify Forms. Submitted fields are stored in our
      Netlify account so our team can review and respond to your request.
      Netlify also processes technical information, such as IP addresses and
      request information, to deliver the site, operate its services, and detect
      abuse. Our forms include a hidden spam detection field. See
      <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/">Netlify’s Privacy Statement</a>
      for more about its practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Website checker information</h2>
    <p>
      When automated checks are available, your name, email address, and website
      URL are also sent through a Netlify function to our website checker backend.
      The checker scans public website pages and generates findings about links,
      search visibility, content, and other website features. The resulting
      report contains information derived from that public website.
    </p>
    <p>
      The checker uses a cookie named <code>kelp_website_checks</code> to track
      free-check usage. Our proxy also forwards your IP address to the checker
      backend to help enforce usage limits and prevent abuse. We save your
      request and report information so we can help you with the findings.
      The report response excludes your submitted name and email address.
      Treat your report link as private: anyone you give the link to may be able
      to view the website findings. The report’s sharing button sends a request
      to share the report with Kelp before opening meeting booking.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We use Google Analytics 4 to understand how visitors use this website and
      improve its content and performance. It uses cookies, including
      <code>_ga</code> cookies, and collects information about pages viewed,
      interactions, referring sources, browser and device characteristics, and
      approximate location. Google processes IP addresses to derive location
      information; Google Analytics 4 does not log or store individual IP addresses.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can read about
      <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245">Google Analytics data practices</a>
      and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s Privacy Policy</a>.
      You can block or delete cookies in your browser and use the
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
      Blocking cookies may affect features such as website checker usage tracking or meeting booking.
    </p>

    <h2>Meeting booking and embedded content</h2>
    <p>
      Our scheduling tool is provided by HubSpot. When it loads or you book a
      meeting, HubSpot processes the information you submit and may collect
      technical information or use cookies to operate the booking experience.
      See <a href="https://legal.hubspot.com/privacy-policy">HubSpot’s Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some pages include content or media delivered by other providers, such as
      WordPress.com image and video services, Gravatar comment avatars, YouTube,
      or Vimeo. When your browser requests that content, the provider receives
      technical information such as your IP address and browser information,
      and may use cookies according to its own privacy policy. Links to other
      websites take you to services governed by their own privacy policies.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <p>
      We use information to respond to inquiries, discuss and provide requested
      services, schedule meetings, generate website reports, follow up on your
      requests and findings, and manage blog comments. We also use technical
      information to operate and improve the site, understand visitor activity,
      prevent spam and misuse, and meet applicable legal obligations.
    </p>

    <h2>Who receives information</h2>
    <p>
      Our team and service providers receive information needed for their roles.
      These include Netlify for hosting and forms, Google for analytics, HubSpot
      for scheduling, our WordPress and website checker systems, and providers
      that support our communications and website content. Public comments and
      report links you share can also make information available to others as described above.
    </p>
    <p>We may disclose information when required by law or a valid legal request,
      or when necessary to protect our rights, visitors, or services.</p>

    <h2>Retention and security</h2>
    <p>
      Retention varies by record type and service. Form submissions, booking
      records, communications, and website reports may remain in the systems
      used to handle them. Public comments may remain with the associated article.
      Contact us to ask about a particular record or request its deletion;
      some information may need to be kept for legal obligations or ongoing services.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use safeguards to protect information, but no website, transmission,
      or storage system can guarantee complete security. Our providers may
      process information in the United States or other countries where they
      operate, which may have different privacy laws from your location.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices and requests</h2>
    <p>
      You can choose whether to submit forms, book a meeting, post a comment, or
      request a website check. Depending on where you live and the laws that
      apply, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or obtain a copy
      of your personal information, or to object to or restrict certain uses.
      To make a request, email <a href="mailto:info@kelp.agency">info@kelp.agency</a>.
      We may need to verify your identity before handling it. You may also have
      the right to raise a concern with your local privacy authority.
    </p>

    <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>This website is intended for businesses and people seeking creative
      services, rather than children under 13. If you believe a child has
      provided personal information, contact us so we can address it.</p>

    <h2>Policy updates</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy as our website or practices change. The date
      above identifies the latest revision.</p>

    <h2>Contact Kelp</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions or requests, email
      <a href="mailto:info@kelp.agency">info@kelp.agency</a>, call
      <a href="tel:+13523257688">352-325-7688</a>, or write to:</p>
    <address>Kelp Creative Agency<br />P.O. Box 116<br />Brooksville, FL 34605<br />United States</address>
  </article>
</Layout>

